WIRE.md §4.2, §5.14, SPEC §1: pairs keys are compared through their templates, whatever the bound: a plain key, a key path and another pairs field meeting an expanded key (`dst0{i}` never does: no leading zero).
-- a/a.canon --
package a

local record Pair {
  k: Int
  v: Int
}

local record R {
  params: [Pair](..=1_000_000_000) @json(pairs: ["dst{i}", "val{i}"])
  dst7: Int
  more: [Pair](..=1_000_000_000) @json(pairs: ["ds{i}", "x{i}"])
  deep: Int @json(path: "val999999999.x")
  fine: [Pair](..=1_000_000_000) @json(pairs: ["dst0{i}", "q{i}"])
  twin: [Pair](..=1_000_000_000) @json(pairs: ["dst1{i}", "y{i}"])
}
-- findings.txt --
error[E3316]  a/a.canon:10:3
  wire key dst7 of dst7 collides with params

error[E3316]  a/a.canon:12:3
  the key path of params is a prefix of the key path of deep

error[E3316]  a/a.canon:14:3
  wire key dst10 of twin collides with params

